      "changedIndices": [
        2
      ],
      "affectedText": "Here $r$ is the distance from the center of the sphere to the observation point. Outside the sphere, the field-line pattern is the same as that of a point charge at the center with the same total charge, as shown in Figure 126. A matching line pattern alone does not determine field magnitude: the same total charge and spherical symmetry are also needed. In a homogeneous surrounding medium, the external field is therefore given by the point-charge formula (8-13). The source writes $r\\geq R_0$; at the surface, the following expression means the limiting field approached from outside. In SI units,",
